<figure class="search-journey">
  <figcaption>Three different questions in a technical SEO audit</figcaption>
  <ol>
    <li><span class="journey-stage">CRAWLING</span><strong>Can Google fetch it?</strong><p>Check crawl access and the response. A blocked request limits what Google can see.</p></li>
    <li><span class="journey-stage">INDEXING</span><strong>Can it be included?</strong><p>Check directives, content and canonical signals. Crawling does not guarantee indexing.</p></li>
    <li><span class="journey-stage">SERVING RESULTS</span><strong>Does it answer this search?</strong><p>Google selects relevant results for a query. Indexing does not guarantee a ranking.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="journey-caption">Audit each stage separately. An HTML check alone cannot establish Google’s indexing or ranking decision.</p>
</figure>
